find_theorems — implementation plan
====================================

status: planned (2026-07-09)

references I1..I5 (plans/repl_list). pass-through ("find_theorems" =>
keys ["repl", "query", "max_results"], default 40 in the dispatcher).
NOTE the ML argument order is (id, max_results, query) — the
dispatcher already handles the reordering; wire keys are what
matters. one design decision inherited from mcp_server.py: its
python-side query AUTO-QUOTING (bare term patterns get wrapped in
quotes). we do NOT reimplement that heuristic scala-side — the
description teaches quoting instead; revisit only if e2e shows models
failing at it.

advertised metadata (the builtin table row)
-------------------------------------------

name          find_theorems
description   "Search for theorems visible in the REPL's current
              context. Criteria: name:foo (name pattern, unquoted),
              intro / elim / dest / solves (goal-based, need a
              current goal), simp:\"term\" (simplification rules for
              a term), or \"pattern\" (term pattern). Terms and
              patterns MUST be quoted: \"_ + _\", \"_ @ _\"; name
              patterns are NOT quoted: name:append. Prefix a
              criterion with - to negate it. Examples: name:conjI,
              \"_ + _ = _\", simp:\"True\", -name:foo. Multiple
              criteria are space-separated and conjoined."
              (source: mcp_server.py find_theorems :366 verbatim,
              minus the auto-quoting it performed silently.)
inputSchema   {"type": "object",
               "properties": {
                 "repl": {"type": "string"},
                 "query": {"type": "string"},
                 "max_results": {"type": "integer", "default": 40}},
               "required": ["repl", "query"]}
annotations   {"readOnlyHint": true, "idempotentHint": true,
               "openWorldHint": false}
              (pure search — readOnlyHint refinement family.)
outputSchema  none.

name/argument mapping across the layers
---------------------------------------

  mcp client edge   tools/call "find_theorems",
                    {"repl": "T", "query": "name:conjI"}
  scala builtin row backend.ir("find_theorems", [(repl,T),
                    (query,"name:conjI")] (+ max_results if given))
  ml dispatcher     "find_theorems" -> Ir.find_theorems (get "repl")
                    (get_int_default "max_results" 40) (get "query")
  engine            ir.ML:758 — Find_Theorems.read_query +
                    find_theorems_cmd against the last state's
                    context (goal-aware when mid-proof); out
                    "found N theorem(s) (M displayed):" + one pretty
                    theorem per line

